PHILOSOPHY & TRANSPARENCY
-------------------------
CoreFlow Engine (CFAE System Framework) and CoreFlow Companion are authored and
maintained by Mystivara Creator, built with transparent AI engineering
collaboration (Claude, ChatGPT, and Gemini). Because rooted Android software
requires full user trust, the complete source code is intentionally kept visible
and auditable — without being stingy or closed off to learning — while still
respecting and protecting the author's original work.

1. WHAT YOU MAY FREELY DO (PERMITTED USE)
   - Download, install, and run official CoreFlow Engine & CoreFlow Companion
     builds free of charge on your personal Android devices.
   - Read, inspect, and security-audit every source file in this repository.
   - Build from source for your own personal device testing, research, and
     educational learning.
   - Submit pull requests, bug reports, translations, and ideas back to the
     official repository (https://github.com/mystivara-creator/CoreFlow-Engine).

2. WHAT REQUIRES PRIOR WRITTEN PERMISSION FROM THE AUTHOR
   - Rebranding, renaming, or republishing CoreFlow (or derivative modules/APKs
     built substantially from this codebase) as your own product.
   - Selling, bundling into paid apps/ROMs, monetizing via paywalls/shortlinks,
     or distributing commercial products based on this codebase.
   - Redistributing modified binaries or forks publicly without explicit
     permission and clear attribution to @mystivara-creator.

3. THIRD-PARTY OPEN-SOURCE COMPONENTS
   This project depends on third-party open-source libraries (including Miuix
   Compose, libsu, cxx, AndroidX, React, Tailwind CSS, and Vite) which remain
   governed by their own respective open-source licenses (Apache-2.0, MIT, etc.).

